.TH picontrol_firmware_upload 2type 2026-08-14 "Linux"

.SH NAME
picontrol_firmware_upload \- piControl driver type for uploading new firmware
to expansion module

.SH LIBRARY
piControl device driver ioctl interface

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <piControl.h>"
.sp
.B struct picontrol_firmware_upload {
.BR "    __u32  addr;"
.BR "    __u32  flags;"
.BR "    __u8   rescue_mode_hw_revision;"
.BR "    __u8   padding[15];"
.B };
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
This struct is used as a parameter to
.BR PICONTROL_UPLOAD_FIRMWARE (2)
to update the firmware of an expansion module.

The fields are as follows:

.TP
.I addr
This field contains the address of the expansion module on the piBridge bus.
.TP
.I flags
This field contains flags that change the behaviour of the firmware upload.
.TP
.I rescue_mode_hw_revision
This field contains the hardware revision of the expansion module that the
firmware will be uploaded to.
Only used if
.I PICONTROL_FIRMWARE_RESCUE_MODE
is set in the
.I flags
field.
.TP
.I padding
Padding for future extensions. This field must be zeroed.

.P
The following flags for the
.I flags
field are available:
.TP
.I PICONTROL_FIRMWARE_FORCE_UPLOAD
This flag disables the version check and allows uploading new firmware even if
the expansion module's firmware isn't older than the firmware that is to be
uploaded.
.TP
.I PICONTROL_FIRMWARE_RESCUE_MODE
This flag enables flashing an expansion module with the assumption that it is
in the rescue mode. This requires the
.I rescue_mode_hw_revision
field to be set to the correct hardware revision of the expansion module.

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR ioctl (2),
.BR PICONTROL_UPLOAD_FIRMWARE (2)
